  "question": {
    "text": "The locus of the centre of the circle which makes equal intercepts on the lines <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let center be <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<br />Since it makes equal intercepts on the two given lines<br />Hence, the center is equidistant from both the lines<br />i.e. <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>"
  }
}